Z||000009||TRiAD||12-29-2001||03:13 AM||||Yeah, spoke with Roodney tonight. FOCOA has a few left, they're purely aesthetic, the shifter doesn't even follow the channels, and he does not recommend them. <P>Oh well. Thanks all! At least now I know.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||12-29-2001||07:12 AM||||Yes, the shifter doesnt go up into the slots. But it does shift same as normal. The gate is oversized to allow that. But it does help like at a car show, to make it look authentic. All Ferraris have the chrome gate. I just use park brake and leave it in neutral in shows, so nobody knows. A shifter  with a boot is an instant dead givaway that its replica.||||reg||1
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||12-29-2001||12:33 PM||||I've seen a 328 replica that had a gated shifter plate, and the shifter was in one of the notches.. looked quite nice.. the only problem with the car? it still had a duke in it... not too authentic for a ferrari replica.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
